### 26. **Builder Pattern Best Practices**

- **Immutability-first**
  - Make built types immutable: `private final` fields, `private` constructor, no setters
  - Return defensive, unmodifiable copies for collections (`List.copyOf(...)`, `Set.copyOf(...)`)

- **Null-safety**
  - Annotate all classes with `@NonNullByDefault`
  - Use `@Nullable` for optional fields and builder parameters only
  - Validate non-null/required inputs in `build()` and fail fast with precise messages

- **Structure and naming**
  - Use a nested `public static final class Builder` inside the built type
  - Provide factories: `public static Builder builder(RequiredA a, RequiredB b)` or `builder()` with `withRequiredX(...)`
  - Use `withX(...)` fluent setters; each returns `this`

- **Required vs optional**
  - Capture required fields early (factory or builder constructor) and re-validate in `build()`
  - Avoid encoding “required” as nullable; prefer types that enforce presence

- **Validation**
  - Validate ranges, formats, and cross-field constraints in `build()`
  - Throw `IllegalArgumentException` with actionable messages; use `ValidationUtils` where applicable

- **Collections**
  - Accept collections in the builder; normalize and copy in `build()`
  - Store as unmodifiable; never expose internal mutables

- **Copy/modify ergonomics**
  - Provide `toBuilder()` or `builder(existing)` to support small mutations without exposing mutability

- **Thread-safety**
  - Builders are not thread-safe (document as such); built objects are thread-safe by immutability

- **Equality and debugging**
  - Implement `equals`, `hashCode`, and `toString` on the built type (not on the builder)

- **Usage discipline**
  - Treat builders as single-use; keep `build()` side-effect free (construct, validate, copy)

- **When to use**
  - Prefer builders for objects with many parameters, optional fields, or cross-field validation
  - For simple data types (≤2–3 params), use constructors or static factories

- **Inheritance**
  - Prefer composition for value objects; if inheritance is necessary, use self-referential generics for covariant builder returns

- **Documentation**
  - Add class-level Javadoc (purpose, constraints, usage) and method docs per standards (author/since)

- **Other**
  - First check existing classes, interfaces or enums before creating them
  - Never use inner structures if they can be avoided

```java
// Example (openHAB style): immutable value with nested builder
package org.openhab.core.ai.example;

import org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.NonNullByDefault;
import org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.Nullable;

import java.util.List;
import java.util.Objects;

@NonNullByDefault
public final class ModelConfig {
    private final String modelId;
    private final int maxTokens;
    private final List<String> fallbackModels;
    private final @Nullable String providerHint;

    private ModelConfig(Builder b) {
        this.modelId = b.modelId;
        this.maxTokens = b.maxTokens;
        this.fallbackModels = List.copyOf(b.fallbackModels);
        this.providerHint = b.providerHint;
    }

    public static Builder builder(String modelId) {
        return new Builder(modelId);
    }

    public Builder toBuilder() {
        return new Builder(this);
    }

    public static final class Builder {
        private String modelId;
        private int maxTokens = 2048;
        private List<String> fallbackModels = List.of();
        private @Nullable String providerHint;

        public Builder(String modelId) {
            this.modelId = Objects.requireNonNull(modelId, "modelId");
        }

        public Builder(ModelConfig source) {
            this.modelId = source.modelId;
            this.maxTokens = source.maxTokens;
            this.fallbackModels = source.fallbackModels;
            this.providerHint = source.providerHint;
        }

        public Builder withMaxTokens(int maxTokens) {
            this.maxTokens = maxTokens;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder withFallbackModels(List<String> fallbackModels) {
            this.fallbackModels = Objects.requireNonNull(fallbackModels, "fallbackModels");
            return this;
        }

        public Builder withProviderHint(@Nullable String providerHint) {
            this.providerHint = providerHint;
            return this;
        }

        public ModelConfig build() {
            if (modelId.isBlank()) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("modelId must not be blank");
            }
            if (maxTokens <= 0) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("maxTokens must be > 0");
            }
            return new ModelConfig(this);
        }
    }
}
```

### 28. **Metrics & Monitoring Best Practices**

- **Centralize metrics**
  - Place all metric types and infrastructure under `org.openhab.core.ai.tool.monitoring` with subpackages:
    - `api` (interfaces, keys), `collector` (mutable hot-path recorders), `snapshot` (immutable views), `registry` (OSGi service), `export` (Prometheus/JMX/REST), `health` (health monitors, alerts)
  - Domain packages should only depend on small monitoring APIs/registry; they should not define their own metric classes

- **Collector vs Snapshot pattern**
  - Use thread-safe collectors for recording: `LongAdder` counters, `System.nanoTime()` durations
  - Compute derived values (rates, averages, percentiles) in immutable snapshot value objects; avoid math in collectors
  - Snapshots must be immutable (`private final` fields, no setters) and annotated with `@NonNullByDefault`

- **Capability interfaces (no deep inheritance)**
  - Define small, composable interfaces in `...monitoring.api`:
    - `MetricsSnapshot` (marker; may expose `timestampMs()`)
    - `CountsMetrics` with `total()`, `success()`, `failure()`, default `successRate()`
    - `LatencyMetrics` with `totalDurationNanos()`, default `averageMs(total)`
    - `HealthMetrics` with `healthy()`, `breakerState()`
  - Prefer composition of capabilities in snapshots over base classes

- **Shared value objects**
  - Use small records to share fields without inheritance:
    - `record Counts(long total, long success, long failure)`
    - `record Timing(long totalDurationNanos)`

- **MetricKey (bounded labels)**
  - Identify metric streams by a small key with bounded labels to control cardinality
  - Provide factories in `MetricKeys` for common keys (provider, tool, action)
  - Example:
```java
@org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.NonNullByDefault
public interface MetricKey {
    String kind();
    java.util.Map<String, String> labels();
    default String id() {
        return kind() + "|" + labels().entrySet().stream()
            .sorted(java.util.Map.Entry.comparingByKey())
            .map(e -> e.getKey() + "=" + e.getValue())
            .reduce((a, b) -> a + "," + b).orElse("");
    }
}

public record SimpleMetricKey(String kind, java.util.Map<String, String> labels) implements MetricKey {}

public final class MetricKeys {
    private MetricKeys() {}
    public static MetricKey provider(org.openhab.core.ai.model.api.ModelProviderType provider) {
        return new SimpleMetricKey("provider", java.util.Map.of("name", provider.name()));
    }
    public static MetricKey tool(String toolName) {
        return new SimpleMetricKey("tool", java.util.Map.of("name", toolName));
    }
    public static MetricKey action(String actionName) {
        return new SimpleMetricKey("action", java.util.Map.of("name", actionName));
    }
}
```

- **MetricsRegistry (OSGi service)**
  - Purpose: single source of truth for collectors; enforces taxonomy; enables enumeration for exporters; supports aggregation and lifecycle
  - Minimal API:
```java
@org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.NonNullByDefault
public interface MetricsRegistry {
    ExecutionMetricsCollector executionCollector(MetricKey key);
    ProviderHealthCollector healthCollector(MetricKey key);
    java.util.Collection<MetricKey> keys();
    <S extends MetricsSnapshot> java.util.List<S> snapshots(Class<S> snapshotType);
    void reset(MetricKey key);
}
```
  - Inject the registry via `@Reference` and obtain collectors by `MetricKey`

- **Collector and snapshot example**
```java
@org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.NonNullByDefault
public final class ExecutionMetricsCollector {
    private final java.util.concurrent.atomic.LongAdder total = new java.util.concurrent.atomic.LongAdder();
    private final java.util.concurrent.atomic.LongAdder success = new java.util.concurrent.atomic.LongAdder();
    private final java.util.concurrent.atomic.LongAdder totalDurationNanos = new java.util.concurrent.atomic.LongAdder();

    public void recordExecution(boolean ok, long durationNanos) {
        total.increment();
        totalDurationNanos.add(durationNanos);
        if (ok) { success.increment(); }
    }

    public ExecutionMetricsSnapshot snapshot() {
        long t = total.sum();
        long s = success.sum();
        long d = totalDurationNanos.sum();
        return new ExecutionMetricsSnapshot(new Counts(t, s, Math.max(0, t - s)), new Timing(d), System.currentTimeMillis());
    }
}

@org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.NonNullByDefault
public record ExecutionMetricsSnapshot(Counts counts, Timing timing, long timestampMs)
        implements MetricsSnapshot, CountsMetrics, LatencyMetrics {
    public long total() { return counts.total(); }
    public long success() { return counts.success(); }
    public long failure() { return counts.failure(); }
    public long totalDurationNanos() { return timing.totalDurationNanos(); }
    public double averageMs() { return LatencyMetrics.super.averageMs(total()); }
}
```

- **Domain usage (record only)**
  - Domain services should only record metrics and read snapshots when needed:
```java
@org.osgi.service.component.annotations.Reference private MetricsRegistry metricsRegistry;

void updateMetrics(org.openhab.core.ai.model.api.ModelProviderType provider, String action, boolean ok, long durationNanos) {
    metricsRegistry.executionCollector(MetricKeys.provider(provider)).recordExecution(ok, durationNanos);
    if (action != null && !action.isBlank()) {
        metricsRegistry.executionCollector(MetricKeys.action(action)).recordExecution(ok, durationNanos);
    }
}
```

- **Label discipline and units**
  - Keep labels bounded (`name`, `region`); avoid high-cardinality values (IDs, user input)
  - Document units in names/Javadoc (e.g., `totalDurationNanos`, `durationMs` in snapshots)

- **Testing**
  - Concurrency tests for collectors (no lost updates)
  - Snapshot math tests for edge cases (zero totals)
  - If exposed via REST, JSON round-trip tests for snapshots

- **Integration with existing classes**
  - `ProviderHealthMetrics` and `MonitoringStatistics` remain immutable snapshots under `...monitoring.snapshot`
  - Replace `AtomicLong`-based `ToolMetrics`/`ProviderMetrics` with `...collector` variants using `LongAdder` and `nanoTime`
  - `ToolExecutionService#getMetrics()` should return an aggregated snapshot type built from the registry

### 29. **Context Classes Best Practices**

- **Immutability with builders**
  - Make contexts immutable snapshots; use `toBuilder()` for safe, scoped mutations
  - Annotate with `@NonNullByDefault`; use `@Nullable` only for truly optional fields
  - Validate required fields in `build()`; fail fast with actionable messages

- **Small capability interfaces (compose, don’t inherit deeply)**
  - Define narrow capabilities in a shared API package (e.g., `org.openhab.core.ai.context.api`):
    - `RequestContext` (correlationId, timestamp, deadlineMs)
    - `SecurityContext` (principalId, permissions)
    - `ProtocolContext` (protocol, version)
    - `TracingContext` (traceId, spanId)
    - `LocaleContext` (locale, timezone)
  - Domain contexts (e.g., `ActionContext`, `ToolContext`) implement only relevant capabilities

- **Typed accessors + namespaced attributes**
  - Provide explicit getters for common fields; avoid stringly-typed access for core data
  - Allow extensibility via a namespaced, JSON-serializable attributes map guarded by constants (`ContextKeys.*`)
  - Enforce prefixes and supported value types when adding attributes

- **Canonical fields**
  - Always include `correlationId` (required) and `timestamp` (`Instant`)
  - Prefer `deadlineMs`/`timeoutMs` over ad-hoc timeouts
  - Actor (`principalId`, `permissions`), `privacyLevel` (enum), `locale`, `timezone` as needed

- **Security and logging**
  - Never store secrets/tokens in plain fields; if unavoidable, mark sensitive and exclude from `toString()`
  - Provide `toSafeString()`/`redact()` for logs; avoid logging full attribute maps

- **Thread-safety and size discipline**
  - Contexts are immutable and safe to share across threads
  - Keep them lightweight; do not embed services/OSGi components or heavy objects
  - Bound attribute map size; avoid high-cardinality payloads

- **Lifecycle and propagation**
  - Create at ingress; pass downstream unchanged; derive child variants via `toBuilder()`
  - Propagate `correlationId` across async boundaries

- **Serialization and versioning**
  - Ensure JSON-friendly types; avoid transient internals
  - Add a `version` field where contexts cross module/network boundaries

- **Package organization**
  - `org.openhab.core.ai.context.api`: capability interfaces, `ContextKeys`, shared value objects
  - Domain-specific contexts live in their domain packages (`action`, `tool`, `auth`) and implement shared interfaces
  - Avoid a central base class or a “god” context

- **Testing**
  - Unit-test builders (validation, required fields), immutability, `equals/hashCode`
  - Round-trip tests for `toBuilder()` and any redaction logic
  - If serialized, add JSON round-trip tests

- **Anti-patterns**
  - Mutable public maps; scattered string keys
  - Deep inheritance trees
  - Embedding live service references inside contexts
  - Logging full contexts with sensitive data

```java
// Example: minimal RequestContext capability and ActionContext with builder
package org.openhab.core.ai.context.api;

import org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.NonNullByDefault;
import org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.Nullable;
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.*;

@NonNullByDefault
public interface RequestContext {
    String correlationId();
    Instant timestamp();
    long deadlineMs();
}

@NonNullByDefault
public final class ActionContext implements RequestContext {
    private final String correlationId;
    private final Instant timestamp;
    private final long deadlineMs;
    private final Map<String, Object> attributes;

    private ActionContext(Builder b) {
        this.correlationId = b.correlationId;
        this.timestamp = b.timestamp;
        this.deadlineMs = b.deadlineMs;
        this.attributes = Map.copyOf(b.attributes);
    }

    public static Builder builder(String correlationId) { return new Builder(correlationId); }
    public Builder toBuilder() { return new Builder(this); }

    public String correlationId() { return correlationId; }
    public Instant timestamp() { return timestamp; }
    public long deadlineMs() { return deadlineMs; }
    public Map<String, Object> attributes() { return attributes; }

    public String toSafeString() { return "ActionContext{" + "correlationId=" + correlationId + ", deadlineMs=" + deadlineMs + "}"; }

    public static final class Builder {
        private String correlationId;
        private Instant timestamp = Instant.now();
        private long deadlineMs = 30_000L;
        private Map<String, Object> attributes = new HashMap<>();

        public Builder(String correlationId) { this.correlationId = Objects.requireNonNull(correlationId, "correlationId"); }
        public Builder(ActionContext src) { this.correlationId = src.correlationId; this.timestamp = src.timestamp; this.deadlineMs = src.deadlineMs; this.attributes = new HashMap<>(src.attributes); }

        public Builder withDeadlineMs(long ms) { this.deadlineMs = ms; return this; }
        public Builder withAttribute(String key, Object value) { /* validate key & type */ this.attributes.put(key, value); return this; }

        public ActionContext build() {
            if (deadlineMs <= 0) { throw new IllegalArgumentException("deadlineMs must be > 0"); }
            return new ActionContext(this);
        }
    }
}
```


### 28. **Configuration Management Best Practices (DS + /conf/ai)**

- **Use OSGi DS with typed MetaType**
  - Define `@ObjectClassDefinition` (OCD) and bind via `@Designate(ocd=...)`
  - Implement DS lifecycle: `@Activate` (initial load), `@Modified` (hot-reload), `@Deactivate` (cleanup)

- **Single source of truth service**
  - Expose a domain-scoped `ConfigService` per boundary (e.g., LLM, agents, MCP)
  - Map OCD → immutable domain config objects (builder pattern, validated)
  - Consumers `@Reference` the service; they do not access Config Admin or files directly

- **Multiple sources with clear precedence**
  - Precedence: Environment variables > Config Admin (.cfg) > files under `/conf/ai` (YAML/JSON) > code defaults
  - Merge at the service boundary; publish an atomic immutable snapshot to consumers

- **File-backed resources under `/conf/ai`**
  - Keep typed repositories for content (not keys): `PromptRepository`, `PolicyRepository`, `ModelPresetRepository`
  - Layout examples:
    - `/conf/ai/agents.cfg` (namespaced keys)
    - `/conf/ai/prompts/<agent>/<intent>.yaml`
    - `/conf/ai/policies/*.yaml`
    - `/conf/ai/models/*.yaml`

- **Hot-reload with openHAB WatchService**
  - Register `WatchService` on `/conf/ai` subtrees; on change, re-parse only the affected repository
  - Rebuild and swap the merged config snapshot atomically; avoid partial reads

- **Placement**
  - DS config services: `org.openhab.core.ai.config` (or domain-scoped `...agent.config`, `...tool.config`)
  - Immutable values: `org.openhab.core.ai.model.configuration`
  - File repositories: `org.openhab.core.ai.config.repo` (prompts/policies/models)

- **Validation and safety**
  - Validate in builders: ranges, formats, cross-field constraints; fail fast with actionable messages
  - Validate YAML/JSON schemas; reject invalid or oversized content
  - Mark secrets in OCD as `AttributeType.PASSWORD`; never log secret values

- **Testing**
  - Unit test mapping (OCD → immutable), merge/precedence rules, and validation
  - Integration test DS activation, `@Modified`, and `WatchService` reload paths

- **Do/Don't**
  - Do: keep configs immutable and thread-safe; publish change events if consumers must react immediately
  - Don't: perform file I/O or Config Admin lookups from consumers; avoid free-form maps for typed config

### 27. **Result Classes Best Practices**

- **Immutability and null-safety**
  - Use immutable value objects: `private final` fields, no setters, defensive copies
  - Annotate classes with `@NonNullByDefault`; use `@Nullable` only for truly optional fields
  - Return empty collections instead of `null`; avoid `Optional` in getters in favor of `@Nullable` + docs

- **Consistent shape**
  - Include a status enum (e.g., `SUCCESS`, `FAILURE`, `PARTIAL`) and helpers like `isSuccess()`
  - Prefer machine-readable fields (enums/typed codes) over free-form text
  - Separate payload from metadata (status, errors, metrics)

- **Errors and diagnostics**
  - Provide `errorCode` (enum), human `message`, optional structured `details`/`hint`
  - Add traceability: `correlationId`/`requestId`, optional `source`
  - Store safe `causeMessage` strings; avoid retaining `Throwable` instances

- **Timing and metrics**
  - Include `timestamp` and optional `durationMs` when representing operations
  - Keep metrics optional and non-intrusive

- **Collections and serialization**
  - Store unmodifiable copies (`List.copyOf(...)`, `Set.copyOf(...)`); never expose mutables
  - Keep fields REST/JSON friendly (simple types, enums); avoid transient internals

- **Equality and debugging**
  - Implement `equals`, `hashCode`, and concise `toString` (omit sensitive/large fields)
  - Define equality semantics (e.g., exclude metrics) and keep consistent

- **Construction API**
  - Provide static factories like `success(...)`, `failure(...)`, `partial(...)`
  - Use a nested `Builder` only when parameters are many or cross-field validation is complex

- **No side effects**
  - Result types should not log or perform I/O; log at call sites

- **Extensibility**
  - For families of results, use an interface or sealed hierarchy for shared fields; prefer composition otherwise

- **Testing**
  - Test success/failure/partial cases, equality contract, and (if applicable) JSON round-trip

```java
package org.openhab.core.ai.result;

import org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.NonNullByDefault;
import org.eclipse.jdt.annotation.Nullable;

import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Objects;

@NonNullByDefault
public final class OperationResult<T> {
    public enum Status { SUCCESS, FAILURE, PARTIAL }
    public enum ErrorCode { NONE, VALIDATION, AUTH, TIMEOUT, INTERNAL }

    private final Status status;
    private final @Nullable T payload;
    private final ErrorCode errorCode;
    private final String message;
    private final List<String> warnings;
    private final String correlationId;
    private final Instant timestamp;
    private final long durationMs;

    private OperationResult(
            Status status,
            @Nullable T payload,
            ErrorCode errorCode,
            String message,
            List<String> warnings,
            String correlationId,
            Instant timestamp,
            long durationMs) {
        this.status = Objects.requireNonNull(status);
        this.payload = payload;
        this.errorCode = Objects.requireNonNull(errorCode);
        this.message = Objects.requireNonNull(message);
        this.warnings = List.copyOf(warnings);
        this.correlationId = Objects.requireNonNull(correlationId);
        this.timestamp = Objects.requireNonNull(timestamp);
        this.durationMs = durationMs;
    }

    public static <T> OperationResult<T> success(T payload, String correlationId, long durationMs) {
        return new OperationResult<>(Status.SUCCESS, payload, ErrorCode.NONE, "", List.of(),
                correlationId, Instant.now(), durationMs);
    }

    public static <T> OperationResult<T> failure(ErrorCode code, String message, String correlationId, long durationMs) {
        return new OperationResult<>(Status.FAILURE, null, code, message, List.of(),
                correlationId, Instant.now(), durationMs);
    }

    public static <T> OperationResult<T> partial(T payload, List<String> warnings, String correlationId, long durationMs) {
        return new OperationResult<>(Status.PARTIAL, payload, ErrorCode.NONE, "", warnings,
                correlationId, Instant.now(), durationMs);
    }

    public boolean isSuccess() { return status == Status.SUCCESS; }
    public boolean isPartial() { return status == Status.PARTIAL; }

